Kev Decide Android sample

Model: Kev-0.8B by Jared Palmer (huggingface.co/jaredpalmer/kev-0.8b, tag v1.0 = commit
bf75a6a8848ea6960ff2ed108d9ed44c2941174f), licensed under Apache License 2.0
(licenses/Kev-APACHE-2.0.txt): a rank-16 LoRA and a pointer head on Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B-Base
(revision dc7cdfe2ee4154fa7e30f5b51ca41bfa40174e68), licensed under Apache License 2.0
(licenses/Qwen3.5-APACHE-2.0.txt). The LiteRT graphs, the pointer head file and the tokenizer.json
the app loads are converted or copied from these checkpoints and are installed on the device, not
kept in this source tree.

The request handling, the rows and the answers are Kotlin ports of the author's code
(github.com/jaredpalmer/kev, tag kev-1.0 = commit 6b719c3c3f367295f6ef336f4f751cf5ff970abc, Apache
License 2.0): kev/api.py render, option_text, question_keys, to_record, _normalize,
choice_confidence, score_confidence, round_prob and to_answers, and the request validation of
SystemOneRequest; kev/model.py user_tokens, encode and rows_of (one causal row per question) and
PointerHead in eval mode with the calibration temperature. Changes include float arithmetic that
reproduces CPython's sum and round, graph windows of 512, 1024 and 2048 tokens with rejection of
longer rows instead of truncation, and the head computed on the host from the graph's hidden
states.

The tokenizer follows the published tokenizer.json contract of Hugging Face tokenizers and
transformers (Apache License 2.0; licenses/Tokenizers-APACHE-2.0.txt and
licenses/Transformers-APACHE-2.0.txt): added-token extraction, NFC, the Split pre-tokenizer
regex, the ByteLevel mapping and byte-level BPE.

The debug gate asset app/src/debug/assets/gate_fixtures.json holds the 144 items of SemIf
benchmarks/data/authored144.jsonl (github.com/TheoLeeCJ/SemIf, commit
ca3ba65f142967030ecb453346e94d6f476a69df), Copyright (c) 2026 TheoLeeCJ, licensed under the MIT
License (licenses/SemIf-MIT.txt), together with 12 invented requests. The three example requests
in app/src/main/res/raw/ are invented requests of the same set.

Gradle wrapper files retain their upstream Apache License 2.0 headers.
Retained model, library and fixture licenses are under licenses/.
